cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SkinSim: a Bloch simulation for time-of-flight MR angiography of cutaneous vessels"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Bastian
    family-names: Rapp
    affiliation: "High-Field MR Center, Center for Medical Physics and Biomedical Engineering, Medical University of Vienna, Vienna, Austria"
license: MIT
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-27
abstract: >-
  A Bloch simulation for time-of-flight MR angiography of small, slow-flowing
  vessels in skin at 3 T. Tissue properties are specified as literature-derived
  intervals and propagated by Latin hypercube sampling, so signal, contrast and
  efficiency are returned as distributions. Sequence settings are free
  parameters, supporting grid and continuous search over the protocol space.
keywords:
  - magnetic resonance imaging
  - time-of-flight angiography
  - Bloch simulation
  - skin
  - subcutaneous vessels
